{"agent":"Monster3-DRV-conformance-7267fe","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"`status()` does `fx[\"_meta\"]` and will raise `KeyError` for any present fixture JSON that lacks a `_meta` field. For example, an unlabelled or legacy fixture file containing `{}` makes `load()` return `{}`, then `status({})` crashes the honest-label/gap conformance check instead of returning `UNVERIFIED`. Use `fx.get(\"_meta\", {})` or explicitly map missing `_meta` to `UNVERIFIED` so the suite reports the fixture defect rather than erroring out.","digest":"d336459a4f349bda","location":"tests/harness_conformance/declared.py:54","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/harness_conformance/declared.py:54"},{"chunk":5,"detail":"Running the documented command `python tests/harness_conformance/report.py` from a clean checkout will fail before producing any output. `Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]` resolves to the `tests/` directory, not the repository root, so the subsequent `from ddflow.services import harnessreg as HR` on line 16 searches for `tests/ddflow/services/harnessreg.py`. In the normal repository layout `ddflow` is a top-level package, not a package under `tests/`. Unless `ddflow` is already installed in site-packages or `PYTHONPATH` includes the repository root, this raises `ModuleNotFoundError` immediately. The script should add the repository root (`parents[2]`) for `ddflow` while retaining access to `tests/harness_conformance`.","digest":"8e14c4cbe676799a","location":"tests/harness_conformance/report.py:15","severity":"HIGH","title":"tests/harness_conformance/report.py:15"}],"chunks_total":6,"coverage":"6/6 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":23040,"diff_sha":"b1057eaa5868e93c1e5b75a6db7ce7e6430cbf87ea5ec7fd0194390997712455","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":998.9,"family":"de